hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9076","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour. H, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of his wife On the authority of Hudhayfah’s sister, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and said: “O women, do you not have enough silver? “There is no woman who adorns herself in gold and displays it, but she will be tortured with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9077","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Mansour, speaking, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of his wife, on the authority of Hudhayfah’s sister, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed us and said: “O women, isn’t there something in silver that you adorn? “There is not a woman among you who adorns herself with gold and displays it, but she will be tortured with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9078","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Mansour, speaking, on the authority of my quarters, on the authority of his wife, on the authority of Hudhayfah’s sister, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed us and said: “O women, isn’t it in the silver that you adorn? “There is not a woman among you who adorns herself with gold and displays it, but she will be tortured for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9079","Abdullah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: He told me Mahmoud bin Amr, that the names of Yazid’s daughter told him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman who is permissible, That is to say, with a necklace of gold, an equal amount of fire is placed around her neck, and any woman who places earrings of gold in her ear, God Almighty will place And in her ear there will be something like a stone of fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"9080","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Zaid told me On the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, that Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him, he said: Hubayra’s daughter came To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in her hand was a seal. He said: This is in my father’s letter, that is, huge seals. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made He, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck her hands, so she came to Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining to her about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had done to her. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then Fatima pulled out a gold chain around her neck and said: This is given to me by Abu Hassan. So the Messenger of God entered. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with the chain in her hand. He said: “O Fatima, are you tempted for people to say: The daughter of the Messenger of God, with a chain in her hand?” “From fire?” Then he left and did not sit down, so Fatima sent the chain to the market, so she sold it and bought a boy with its price. Another time: A slave, and he mentioned a word that meant it, so she freed him, so he told about that, and said: “Praise be to God who saved Fatima from the Fire.” Suleiman bin Salam Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumayl told us, he said: Hisham Al-Dastawi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir. On the authority of Abu Salam, whose name is Mutur, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Thawban, he said: Hubayra’s daughter came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And in her hand was a ring of gold, that is, huge rings, and the like."
"9081","Ishaq bin Shaheen Al-Wasiti informed us, saying: Khaled informed us, on the authority of Mutarrif. H And Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, on the authority of Abu Zaid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of God, two bracelets of gold? He said: “Two bracelets of fire.” She said: O Messenger of God, a bracelet of gold? He said: “A ring of fire.” She said: Two rings of gold? He said: “Two rings of fire.” He said: And she was wearing two bracelets of gold, so she threw them and said: O Messenger of God, if a woman does not She dressed herself up for her husband, and she dressed up for him. He said: “What prevents one of you from making two earrings of silver, then decorating them with saffron, or By Abeer, the pronunciation is for Ahmad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9082","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw two gold coins on her, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Shall I not tell you what is better than this? If you took this off and made two holders of paper, then smeared them with saffron.” “They were good.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This has not been preserved, and God knows best."
"9083","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Aflah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Ibn Zurayr, He heard Ali bin Abi Talib say: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took silk and placed it in his right hand, and he took gold and placed it in To his left, then he said: “Indeed, these are forbidden to the males of my nation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9084","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Saabah, on the authority of a man from Hamadan, it is said To him: Abu Aflah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Ibn Zurayr, that he heard Ali bin Abi Talib say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took He took silk, and placed it in his right hand, and he took gold, and placed it in his left, then he said: “Indeed, these are forbidden to the males of my nation.”"
"9085","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Sa’bah, on the authority of a man from Hamadan, called Aflah, on the authority of Ibn Zurayr, that he heard Ali says: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took silk and placed it in his right hand, and he took gold and placed it in his left hand, then he said: “ These two things are forbidden to the remembrance of my nation.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Ibn al-Mubarak is more similar to the authentic hadith than the one before it, and God Almighty knows best, except for his saying: on the authority of He succeeded, for Abu Aflah is more deserving of doing what is right. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9086","Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Al-Saabah, on the authority of Abu Aflah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zurayr Al-Ghafiqi, he said: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took gold in his right hand and silk in his left, and said: “This is forbidden to the males of my nation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9087","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, Yazid, Mu’tamar, and Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, they said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Musa, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has made silk and gold permissible for the females of my nation, and has forbidden them for women.” Her mention \""
9088"""
"9088","'Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Darhami informed us, saying: 'Abdul-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Gold and silk have been permitted for the females of my Ummah, and forbidden for its males."""
"9089","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Muawiyah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, abstain from wearing gold except in pieces."
"9090","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Muawiyah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade wearing gold except in pieces, and riding on horseback.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9091","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Shaykh, that he heard Muawiyah, and he had A group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you know that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade wearing gold except in pieces?” They said: “By God, yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9092","Ahmad ibn Harb informed us, he said: Asbat informed us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Abu Shaykh, he said: While we were with Muawiyah in Some of his arguments, when he gathered a group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to them: Do you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said, “He forbade wearing gold unless it is in pieces?” They said, “By God, yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9093","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: he told me Abu Sheikh Al-Hinai, on the authority of Abu Hamman, that in the year Muawiyah performed Hajj, he gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Kaaba. He said to them: I adjure you by God, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid wearing gold? They said: Yes. He said: So I I bear witness (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9094","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd Al-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi told us Many, he said: Abu Sheikh told me, on the authority of his brother Hamman, that in the year Muawiyah performed Hajj, he gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in The Kaaba, and he said: I adjure you by God, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid wearing gold? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9095","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Saeed told us, he said: Shuaib, who is Ibn Ishaq, told us. He said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Abu Sheikh told me, he said: Jammaz told me, he said: Muawiyah’s Hajj So he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba and said: I adjure you by God, did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding gold? They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And I bear witness.”"
"9096","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Amara bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu told me Ishaq, he said: Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba, and he said: I adjure you by God, have you not heard? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbids gold?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And I bear witness.”"
"9097","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid told us, on the authority of Uqba, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, He said: Ibn Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba, and said: Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Is it forbidden to use gold?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And I bear witness.”"
"9098","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, he said Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba, and he said: I adjure you by God, did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbidding gold?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: “And I “I bear witness.” Al-Nasa’i told us: Qatada has better memory than Yahya bin Abi Kathir, and his hadith is more worthy of authenticity, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9099","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: An-Nadr ibn Shumail informed us, he said: I am Bayhas ibn Fahdan, he said: I am Abu Shaykh al-Hina’i, he said: I heard Muawiyah, and around him were people of the Muhajireen and Ansar, and he said to them: Did you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Wearing silk? They said: Yes. He said: And he forbade wearing gold except in pieces? They said: Yes."
"9100","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told me, he said: Ali bin Ghurab told us, he said: Bayhas bin Fahdan told us, he said: Abu Shaykh told us Al-Hinai, who said: I heard Ibn Omar, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing gold except in pieces.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of al-Nadr ibn Shumayl is more likely to be authentic, and God Almighty knows best."
"9101","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Salam bin Zurayr told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Tarfa told us, on the authority of his grandfather Arfajah bin Asaad said that his nose was injured on the Day of the Dogs in pre-Islamic times, so he made a nose out of paper, and it stank on it. So the Prophet ordered him to May God bless him and grant him peace, to have a nose of gold.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9102","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yazid, who is Ibn Zurai’, told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Tarfa told me, On the authority of Arfaja bin Asaad bin Kurayb, he said: He was his grandfather. He said: He told me that he saw his grandfather, whose nose was injured on the Day of the Killing. Pre-Islamic times, he said: So he took a nose of silver, and it became stench. He said: “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to make it of gold.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9103","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad bin Kathir al-Harrani told us, saying: Sa`id bin Hafs told us, he said: I am Musa bin Ayan, on the authority of Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Omar said to Suhayb: “What do I think about you? The gold ring? He said: Someone better than you saw it, and he did not care about it. He said: Who is it? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9104","Ali bin Hajar informed us, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger took God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a gold ring, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wore it. Then the people took gold rings, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I used to wear this ring, but I will never wear it again.” So he threw it away, and the people threw away their rings."
"9105","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra bin Yarim, he said: Ali said: “He forbade me The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the golden seal, on the authority of the bow, on the authority of the mitre, and on the beer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9106","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Ali. He said: “The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the golden seal, on the authority of the bowstring, and on the footsteps of donkeys.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9107","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Hubayra, he heard it from Ali, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the gold ring, the red mitre, and the Hard clothes, and about beer, “a drink made from barley and wheat. He recalled his distress (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9108","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Sa`sa`ah bin Suhan, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from using the gold ring, the bowstring, and the mithra And beer.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The one before it is more like the correct one. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9109","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Ubayd Allah bin Musa, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Malik bin Umair, On the authority of Sa`sa’a bin Suhan, he said: I said to Ali: He forbade us from doing what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade. He said: “He forbade me from creeping creatures. And the hattam, and the gold ring, and the silk garment, and the bowstring, and the red mithra.”"
"9110","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaym told us, he said: Marwan told us, he is the son of Muawiyah, he said: Ismail told us, he is the son of Sami’. Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Malik bin Umair, said: Sa’sa’a bin Suhan came to Ali and said: He forbade us from what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade. And peace be upon him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from lizards, hantam, naqir, and al-ja’ah, and he forbade us from engaging in gold, a garment of silk, a bow’s garment, and a red mitre.”"
"9111","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid, who is Ibn Ziyad, told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, he said: Malik bin Umair told us, He said: Sa’saa bin Suhan said to Ali: O Commander of the Faithful, forbid us from doing what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us. He said: “He forbade us.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of beasts of war, and on the hentam, and on the beer, and on the authority of shaving gold, and on the wearing of silk, and on the mithra. “The red one.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: The hadith of Marwan and Abd al-Wahid is more correct than the hadith of Israel."
"9112","Muhammad bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far Ghandar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Hunayn, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I was forbidden from wearing red clothes and a gold ring, and from reciting Qur’an while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9113","Abu Dawud informed us. He said: Abu Ali al-Hanafi and Uthman ibn Umar told us. Abu Ali said: He told us. Uthman said: Dawud informed us. Bin Qais, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali, who said: “My beloved, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade me.” And he said nothing about three things. I do not say he forbade the people. He forbade me: from sealing gold, from wearing iron, from clothed clothes and from clean clothes, and not I recite prostrating, not kneeling.”"
"9114","Al-Hasan bin Dawud Al-Mankadri told us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me, and I do not say he forbids you, about stamping gold. “And about wearing straight clothes, and about wearing combed and shrouded clothing, and about reciting while bowing.”"
"9115","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a gold ring, and from reciting while bowing. “And on the authority of the hardwood, and on the authority of the safflower.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9116","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Abu Al-Aswad told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Yunus, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibrahim, that his father told him that he heard Ali say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from “Reciting while bowing, and about wearing gold and brocade.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9117","Issa bin Hammad told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid, that Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn narrated to him, that his father narrated to him, that He heard Ali say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a gold ring, from wearing coarse and saffron clothing, and from reading the Qur’an. And I was kneeling.”"
"9118","Al-Hasan bin Qazah Al-Basri told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah Ibn Hunayn, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Ali saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me, and I do not say he forbids you, about Khatim “Gold, and on copper, and on taffy, and to recite the Qur’an while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9119","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, and he said again: I am Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me, and said Once again: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “wearing coarse and taffy cloth, stamping gold, and reading in Kneeling.” He said again: “And about reciting the Qur’an while bowing.”"
"9120","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Isa, he said: Zayd bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim Mawla Ali, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from stamping gold, from saffron, and from wearing iron.” “And about reciting while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9121","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Hunayn, Ibn Abbas’s client, that Ali said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a bow. “And of the saffron, and of the sealing with gold.”"
"9122","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Hunayn. Mawla Ali, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from four things: from sealing gold, and from “I wear hard clothing, and when I recite the Qur’an while bowing, and when I wear saffron.”"
"9123","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Hafs bin Abdul Rahman Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of a client of Abbas, that Ali said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing saffron, and from “I should wear the traditional clothing, abstain from wearing rings with gold, and abstain from reciting while bowing.”"
"9124","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, he said: Harb told us, and he is Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya He said: Amr bin Saad Al-Fadaki told me, that Nafi’ told him, he said: Ibn Hunayn told me, that Ali told him, he said: “He forbade me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked for saffron clothing, for a gold ring, for wearing a bow, and for me to recite while bowing.”"
"9125","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of some of the people of Al-Abbas, on the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the use of saffron and harsh clothes, and of reciting while \kneeling\"""""
"9126","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Muhammad bin Ibrahim told him, on the authority of Ibn Hunayn, on the authority of Ali, that he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from four things: from wearing a yellow garment, and from wearing one’s ring. with a gold ring, and to wear a Qibi, and to recite the Qur’an while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9127","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told me, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Khalid bin Ma’dan told me, that Ibn Hunayn told him that Ali said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the wearing of saffron clothes and silk, and that one should recite He was kneeling, and he was wearing a gold ring.” Abu Nu'aym disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Hunayn, and he did not mention Khaled. Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abu Nu`aym, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Hunayn, that Ali told him, Like it. Al-Awza'i sent him. Mahmoud bin Khaled told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr, meaning Al-Awza’i, told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ali, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me.” The hadith is narrated, mursal"
"9128","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, he said: “He forbade me The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of a bow, silk, and a gold ring, and to recite while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9129","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, he said: “He forbade \The purple garment"
"9130","Ahmad bin Hafs told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, he is the son of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Bashir ibn Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “about sealing gold”"
"9131","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “forbade the use of a gold ring.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Shu`bah is more authentic than the hadith of al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9132","Yusuf bin Hammad Al-Ma’ni Al-Basri told us, he said: Abd Al-Warith told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, he said: Hafs Al-Laythi told us, he said: I bear witness to Imran that, he told us, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from wearing silk, and from wearing rings with gold. And about drinking in hanams.”"
"9133","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Bakr bin Sawadah, that Abu al-Najib al-Bakhtari told him that Abu Sa`id al-Khudri told him that a man came from Najran to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he was wearing a gold ring. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him and said: “You came to me with an ember of fire in your hand.”"
"9134","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of a man, he told him, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, that a man was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was wearing a gold ring, and on the hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace A piece of paper, or a newspaper, and he struck the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his finger with it, and the man said: What is the matter with me, O Messenger of God? He said: “Won’t you throw away this that is on your finger?” So the man took it and threw it away. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw it after that and said: “What? What about the ring? He said: I threw it away. He said: I did not order you to do this. I only ordered you to sell it and use its price. Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9135","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a gold ring on his hand, and he began to knock on it with a rod. With him, when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, neglected to meet him, he said: “We did not see anything but that we had caused you pain and fined you.” Yunus disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris, with a mursal message. Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu told me Idris Al-Khawlani, “A man among those who accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wore a gold ring,” similar to what Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: The hadith of Yunus is more likely to be authentic than the hadith of al-Numan, and God knows best. Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi informed us. Abu Abd al-Malik, a reading, said: Ibn Aidh narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “saw a man wearing a gold ring,” and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9136","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abdul Aziz Al-Omari told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “saw a gold ring on a man’s hand, so he struck his finger with a rod he had with him until he threw it away.” Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ali Al-Marwazi told me, he said: Al-Warkani told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This mursal is more like the correct one, and God Almighty knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9137","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muslim from the people of Mur and Abu Taybah told me, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing an iron ring, and he said: “What do I see? “Do you wear the jewelry of the people of Hell?” So he threw it away, then he came to him, wearing a ring made of something similar to it, and said: “Why do I find the smell of idols coming from you?” So he threw it away He said: O Messenger of God, from what should I take it? He said: “Take it from paper, and do not complete it with a mithqal.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9138","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, Ishaq bin Bishr informed us Ibrahim, Ali bin Hajar, and the pronunciation for him, they said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “We have made a seal and engraved an inscription on it, so no one will inscribe it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9139","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fabricated A ring, and he said: “We have taken a ring and engraved an inscription on it, so no one should inscribe it.” And I saw its sparkle on the little finger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9140","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He took a paper signet, the ring of which was Ethiopian.”"
"9141","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “took a seal of paper, with an Ethiopian ring on it, and on it was engraved: Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9142","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Abbad bin Musa told us, he said: Talha bin Yahya told us, he said: Yunus bin Yazid told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a silver ring, which he used to seal his right hand. An Ethiopian lobe, and he makes his lobe from what follows his palm.”"
"9143","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who is Ibn Salih, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The seal of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was made of silver, and a portion of it was made of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9144","Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalid Al-Homsi told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Salamah, who is the son of Abdul-Malik Al-Awsi, told us on the authority of Al-Hasan, who is Ibn Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Humaid al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He was “the seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” peace be upon him, of silver, and his portion was of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9145","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Umayyah bin Bastam told us, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: I heard Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “his seal was made of paper, and his mouth was made of paper.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9146","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Musa bin Dawud, the judge of Al-Thaghr, told us, he said: Zuhayr bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, He said: “The seal of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was made of silver, and a piece of it was made of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9147","Muhammad bin Amir told us, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “seal his seal in his right hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9148","Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami told us, he said: Sallam bin Qutaybah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “It is as if I Look at the whiteness of the ring of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his left finger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9149","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: He wanted The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked to write to the Romans, and they said: They do not read a letter unless it is sealed. He said: “So he took a silver ring. It is as if I were looking at the whiteness of it in his hand, and inscribed on it: “Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9150","Ahmad bin Uthman Al-Basri Abu Al-Jawza told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Qurra bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the last evening prayer until half the night had passed, then he went out and led us in prayer. “It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of his silver ring on his hand.”"
"9151","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Thabit told us, that they asked Anas about The seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “It is as if I were looking at the gleam of his silver ring, and he raised his left little finger.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than what was narrated on the authority of Anas, and God knows best"
"9152","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Sulaiman, he is Ibn Bilal, on the authority of Sharik Ibn Abi Nimr, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abd. Allah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali. A partner said, and Abu Salamah told me, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to wear his ring on his right hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9153","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Basri Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rafi’. On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “seal his oath” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9154","Amr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Abu Attab Sahl bin Hammad Al-Basri. And Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Attab told us, he said: Abu Makin Nuh ibn Rabi’ah told us, Iyas ibn al-Harith ibn al-Muqayb told us. On the authority of his grandfather Mu’aqib, he said: “The seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was made of twisted iron, with silver on it.” He said: Al-Mu'aqib was the seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The pronunciation is by Abu Dawud"
"9155","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali Al-Masisi told me, he said: Dawud bin Mansour told us, from the people of Al-Thaghr, trustworthy 5, he said: Laith told us Ibn Saad, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Bakr Ibn Sawada, on the authority of Abu Al-Najib Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: “ A man from Bahrain came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he greeted him, but he did not respond to him. He had a gold ring in his hand and a meal. He returned them to him, then said: O Messenger of God, I came to you just now, but you turned away from me. He said: “It was in me.” Your hand is an ember of fire.” He said: “Then I have brought many coals.” He said: “As for what you have brought, it is no more sufficient for us than the stones of the heat. But it is an enjoyment of the life of this world.” He said: “What shall I seal?” He said: “An iron ring, or paper, or a scratch.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9156","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, he said: Abdullah told me Al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and took a silver ring, and said: “Who If he wants to engrave it, let him do so, but do not inscribe its inscription.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9157","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif Al-Basri told us, he said: Harun bin Ismail Basri told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us Basri, who said: Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a ring and engraved it. There was an inscription on it. He said: “We have taken a ring and engraved an inscription on it, so no one should inscribe an inscription on it.” Then Anas said: It is as if I I look at him, and his light is in his hand."
"9158","Mujahid bin Musa Al-Khwarizmi told us, in Baghdad, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, on the authority of Azhar bin Rashid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not illuminate the fire of polytheism, and do not engrave on your rings \Arabic\"""""
"9159","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: Ali said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Ali, ask God for guidance and protection, and he forbade me from putting the seal on this and that, and he pointed, meaning with his index finger.” And the middle \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9160","Hanad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me.” May God bless him and grant him peace, that I may be sealed on this finger of mine, and on the middle finger, or the next one.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it."
"9161","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a ring on this and that,” meaning: the index and middle fingers. The wording is by Ibn al-Muthanna (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9162","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: I heard Ali, He says: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a ring on my index and middle fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9163","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Ali, he said: he told me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Say, ‘O God, guide me and guide me’,” and he forbade me from putting a ring on this or that, and Bishr indicated With the index and middle fingers. He said: And Asim said: One of them"
"9164","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Saeed, who is Ibn Amir, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “take off his ring when he entered the toilet.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith is not preserved, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9165","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Shaybani, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a ring and put it on. He said: “This has distracted me from you.” Since today, a look to him, and a look to you.” Then he threw him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9166","Muhammad bin Sulaiman Luwayn told us, in reading, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, “He saw in the hand of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a paper ring one day, so they made it and put it on. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, threw it away, and the people threw it away.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9167","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fabricated A ring of gold, and he used to wear it, so he placed the center of it on the inside of his hand, and people did so. Then he sat on the pulpit, took it off, and said: “I “I used to wear this ring, and I used to make a ring on the inside.” He threw it away, then said, “By God, I will never wear it again.” The people shunned it. Their rings"
"9168","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Al-Mu`tamir, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God took May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he wore a gold ring, and he placed the center of it on the front of his palm, so the people took gold rings, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, threw He handed over his ring and said, “I will never wear it.” And the people threw away their rings."
"9169","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, May God bless him and grant him peace. He took a ring of gold and made its part from what follows his palm. So the people took rings, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, threw it away. He said: “I will never wear it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9170","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Bishr, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah took May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he wore a gold ring, and he made the center of it from what follows the inside of his palm, so the people took the rings, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave it to him. He said: “I will never wear it.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a paper ring and put it in his hand. In the hands of Abu Bakr, then it was in the hands of Omar, then it was in the hands of Uthman until he perished in Bir Aris. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9171","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to put a gold ring on it, then put it down, and put on a paper ring, and Muhammad, the Messenger of God, was engraved on it. He said: “No one should engrave the inscription of my ring on this,” and he placed the blade on the inside of his palm. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9172","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Ziyad Al-Mawsili, he said: Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wore a gold ring for three days, and when his companions saw it, the gold rings scattered on them, so he threw it away. We do not know what he did. Then he ordered a silver ring to be engraved on it, and it was in the hands of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Until he died, and in the hand of Abu Bakr until he died, and in the hand of Omar until he died, and in the hand of Othman for six years of his work, and when the books on him multiplied, He gave it to a man from the Ansar, and he used to seal it with it. Then the Ansari went out to Uthman’s cell, and it fell. He looked for it but was not found, so he ordered With a similar seal, and inscribed on it is Muhammad, the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9173","Qutaibah told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, When he greeted, he took a ring of gold, and he used to place the ring on the inside of his hand, so the people took rings of gold, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, threw him away. May God bless him and grant him peace, so the people took off their rings, and he took a silver ring, and he used to seal it with it, but he did not wear it.”"
"9174","Muhammad bin Othman Al-Basri Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Wazir Basri told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Omar Al-Jumahi told us, On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Sheikh, he said: I was sitting with Salem, when a group of Umm al-Banin passed by us, and they had bells, so Salem spoke to Nafi’. On the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Angels do not accompany them on rides, with a jingle with them.” How many jingles do you see with these people? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9175","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is the son of Harun, he said: Nafi’ bin Omar told us. Al-Jumahi, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Musa, said: I was with Salem bin Abdullah, and he narrated, Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said, “The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a rattle.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9176","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham Al-Makhzoumi told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Omar told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Musa, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, raised it up, and said: “Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a rattle.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9177","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman bin Babih, a servant, told me Abu Nawfal, that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Do not enter “The angels have a house in which there is a bell, and the angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Suleiman bin Babih: The oldest sheikh who heard from Ibn Jurayj from the people of Mecca. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9178","Abu Kurayb Muhammad bin Al-Alaa Abu Kurayb told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father, said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw me ragged clothes, so he said: “Do you have any money?” I said: Yes. O Messenger of God, of all wealth. He said: “If God gives you wealth, let him see its effect on you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9179","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father, He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing a thin garment, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you have any money?” He said: Yes, of all money. He said: “From what money?” He said: “God has given me camels, sheep, horses and slaves.” He said: “So if God has given you money, let its effect be seen on you.” God’s grace and honor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9180","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yazid, who is Al-Wasiti, told us, he said: I am Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father, said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw him in a bad appearance, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you have any wealth?” He said: I said: Yes, of all the wealth God has given me. He said: “If you have wealth, let it be seen on you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9181","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi told us, he said: Abu al-Nadr told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Zur’ah, on the authority of Muhajir al-Shami, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears a garment of fame in this world, God will clothe him with a garment humiliation in the hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9182","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aisha, “It is She made a black cloak made of wool for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he put it on. When he sweated and felt the smell of the wool, he threw it away, and he loved a good smell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9183","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: Ali said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Ali, ask God for guidance and guidance,” and He forbade me from using a red mitre, and from using a bow. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9184","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Burdah, he said: I heard Ali, saying: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from using the bow and the mitre.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith of Shu`bah is correct, and the one before it is wrong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9185","Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya Maruzi told us, saying: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ata’, and he is Ibn Al-Sa’ib On the authority of Abu Jadham, that Abu Ja`far told them, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade On the authority of three: “He forbade me from wearing rings with gold, and he forbade me from wearing a loose garment, and he forbade me from reciting the Qur’an while bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9186","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali, he said: “He forbade me Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I do not say that we forbid you from wearing a ring with gold, or reciting while bowing, or prostrating, or wearing bow, or ride on a red harp.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9187","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, and Abu Amir, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Awn Al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Abu Saleh al-Hanafi, whose name is Mahan, says: I heard Ali saying: I gave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a suit of Shira, so he sent it to me. So I put it on, and I saw the anger on his face. He said: “But I did not give it to you to wear.” So he ordered me, so I put it around among my wives. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Thus, Ishaq said: Dishonored, and what is correct is that Abd al-Rahman bin Qays is the brother of a freed man. It was narrated by Shu’bah on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ali"
"9188","Muhammad ibn Bashar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad Ghandar narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, clothed me with the robe of Shira’, so I went out in it, and I saw anger on his face, so I divided her among my wives.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9189","Issa Hammad bin Zaghba Al-Basri told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid, that Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn told him, that His father told him that he heard Ali saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a gold ring, and from wearing the cloth of a cloth and clothed hair. And reciting the Qur’an while I was kneeling, and he clothed me with a garment from Shira, so I went out in it, and he said to me: “O Ali, I did not clothe her so that you could wear it.” So I returned to Fatima and gave it to her, as if it were folded with me, so I tore it apart, and she said: May your hands be shattered, O Ibn Abi Talib, what you brought. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing it, so wear it and clothe your wives.”"
"9190","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the market, leaning on it, and I saw a beautiful garment being sold in the market, so I said: O Messenger of God, if only You bought this and used it to beautify yourself for the Arab delegations when they came to you, and when you addressed the people on the day of Eid and other days. He said: “He only wears “This is someone who has no morals.” So he stayed as long as God willed, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was given a robe of Shira’, and he sent it to me. So I left in horror when I heard from him, and no message with it to me, so I said: O Messenger of God, you send this to me in this condition, and I heard you say Concerning what you said: He said: “I only sent it to you so that you could clothe it, or sell it and spend its price. I did not send it to you so that you could wear it.” So Omar sent her to the market (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9191","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said that he saw a piece of clothing being sold at the door of the mosque, so I said: O Messenger of God, if I bought this for Friday And for the delegation when they come to you, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is only worn by he who has no share in the Hereafter,” he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought some of her clothes, and he clothed me with one of them, and she said: O Messenger of God, you clothed me with her, and you said Concerning what you said, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I did not clothe her so that she could wear it, but I clothed her so that you could clothe her, or to sell her.” So Omar, his brother on his mother’s side, was a polytheist. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9192","Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman On the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Omar told him that Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a garment made of silk, and he said: O Messenger of God, if Did you buy this suit and wear it to the delegation and on Friday? He said: “This is only worn by one who has no clothing in the Hereafter.” After that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a suit to Omar. A silk robe. He covered it with her, and Omar said: O Messenger of God, you clothed her with me, and I heard you say about it what you said. So he said: “Sell it or sell it.” \You clothe it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9193","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Salem bin Abdul God, he said: I heard Ibn Omar, speaking, that Omar, went out and saw an Istabraq suit being sold in the market, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: O Messenger of God, buy it and wear it on Friday, when the delegation comes to you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These are worn only by those who have no manners.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with three of these suits. They clothed Omar with a suit, and with a suit. Ali wore a suit, and he covered Osama with a suit, so he came to him and said: O Messenger of God, you said about it what you said, then you sent to me! He said: “Sell it and fulfill your needs with it, or share it as wine among your wives.” Imran bin Musa Basri told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Abi Ishaq, told us, he said: Salem said: What is Istibraq? I said: What is thicker than the brocade, and coarse than it? He said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar saying: Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a man wearing a silk garment. He brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, buy this, and he narrated the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9194","Ubayd Allah bin Faddala told us, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: I am Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem bin Abdullah told me, that Abdullah bin Omar, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab found a suit of Istabraq being sold in the market, so he took it and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him. He greeted him and said: O Messenger of God, buy this and decorate it for the Eid and for the delegation. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “These are only “The clothing of one who has no manners.” So Omar stayed as long as God wished for him to stay, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him with a brocade suit, and he accepted. Omar carried it until the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought it and said: O Messenger of God, you said: This is the clothing of one who has no clothing. Then you sent He brought this robe to me, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You sell it, or you fulfill your need with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9195","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, saw the Shira’a suit of Atarid bin Hajib Al-Tamimi being sold, so he said: O Messenger of God, buy This suit is to be worn on Friday, and if the delegation comes, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Only those who do not wear this suit will wear it.” A reward for him in the Hereafter.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought from it and sent to Omar ibn al-Khattab from it, and Omar said: How should I wear it when you said what you said about it? He said: “I did not clothe her so that she could wear it, but rather sell it or clothe her.” So Omar sent it to a brother of his from the people of Mecca before he He greets (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9196","Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I saw on Zainab The daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a silk shirt, Siraa. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9197","Amr bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Baqiya, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he told me that: He saw on Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the garment of Sira’, and Sira’ means the one lined with silk. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it, and God grant us success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9198","Imran bin Bakkar Al-Humsi told us, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: I am Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, he said: Al-Zuhri was asked: Does he wear Silk women, or not? He said: Anas bin Malik told me that he “saw on Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a Sira’a silk cloak.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9199","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab said, Anas bin Malik told me that he “saw on a mother Kulthum, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a silk cloak from Sira’."
"9200","Muhammad bin Ismail told us, he said: I am Ayoub bin Sulayman, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, he said: Yahya said: Ibn Shihab: Anas bin Malik told me that he “saw the hail of Shira’ on Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9201","Saeed bin Amr Al-Homsi told us, he said: Baqiya bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “did not see any harm in women’s silk or silk.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said to me: This is objectionable from the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9202","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Ismail bin Aliya, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the hereafter.”"
"9203","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr while he was on the pulpit delivering a sermon, and he said : Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9204","Amr bin Yazid Basri informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us. H And Muhammad bin Abbad bin Adam told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Maimun, on the authority of Khalifa bin Ka’b, he said: He addressed us Ibn Al-Zubayr, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and whoever does not wear it In the Hereafter, he will not enter Paradise, God said: And their clothing therein will be silk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9205","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, he said: Khalifa told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr. He delivers a sermon, saying: Do not wear your women with silk, for I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears it In this world, he will not wear it in the Hereafter.” Ibn al-Zubayr said: Whoever wears it in this world will not enter Paradise. God Almighty said: Their clothing is silk"
"9206","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abu Dhubyan, he said: He addressed us. Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: “Do not wear silk, for whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the hereafter.” Ibn Umar said: “Then, by God, no He will enter Paradise. God Almighty said: “And their clothing therein will be silk.”"
"9207","Ubayd Allah ibn Fadalah told me. He said: I am Abu Muammar. He said: Abdul-Warith told us. He said: He increased al-Qassam and he increased bribery. He told us: Mu'adh said: The mother of Amr bint Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told me that she heard from Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, saying in his sermon: He heard it from Omar, saying: He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever wears silk in this world, it will not be clothed in the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9208","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Ali bin Ubaid al-Tanafisi, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, meaning Ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abdullah Mawla Asmaa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: Omar told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Who He who wears silk in this world will not wear it in the hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9209","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi informed us, saying: Abdah ibn Sulayman, who is Kufi, told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Abdullah Mawla Asma, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world, will not He will wear it in the afterlife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9210","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, he said: I am Harb bin Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: He told me Imran bin Hattan, that he asked Abdullah bin Abbas about wearing silk, and he said: Ask Aisha about it, so I asked Aisha, and she said: Ask Abdullah bin Omar, and he said: Abu Hafs told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world, there is no good for him.” for him in the Hereafter.”"
"9211","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, and Bishr bin Aidh. On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Only someone who has no manners wears silk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9212","Suleiman bin Salam Al-Balkhi Abu Dawud Al-Masafifi told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Bakr ibn Abd God, and give good tidings to Ibn Muhtafiz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Only someone who has no clothing wears silk.”"
"9213","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Abu Al-Numan told us in the year two hundred and seven, he said: Al-Saqq bin Hazan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ali. Al-Bariqi, he said: A woman came to me and asked me a fatwa, and I said to her: This is Ibn Umar, so I followed him asking him, and I followed her, listening to what he was saying. She said: Could you give me a fatwa about silk? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it.” Brief. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Nu`man’s name is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl, and his surname was A’im, and he mixed together at the end of his life. Sulayman ibn Harb: If Abu al-Nu`man agrees with me, I do not care who disagrees with me, meaning Aram. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He was one of the trustworthy people before that. He mixes (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9214","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ali al-Bariqi, he said: A woman asked Ibn Omar said: “About jewellery, so he made a concession on it.” I asked him: “About silk, but he disapproved of it.” The woman said: Is it forbidden? He said: We were talking about the fact that “whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9215","Abu Bakr bin Ali Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Surayj told us, and he is Ibn Yunus, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf bin What is wrong with you? He said: I asked Ibn Umar’s woman: “About gold. Should I wear it?” He said: Yes. She said: And silk? He said: He dislikes silk. Then he said in Third: Silk. He said: Whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the hereafter."
"9216","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Nafi told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Yunus Hatim bin Muslim bin Abi Saghira, he said: I heard a servant of Quraysh say: A woman came to Ibn Umar and said: “What do you say about silk?” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. “Peace be upon him”"
"9217","Ibrahim Ibn Al-Hasan Al-Maqsimi told me, he said: Hajjaj Ibn Muhammad told us, he said: I heard Shu’bah, speaking on the authority of Yunus Ibn Muslim Ibn Abi Little, that a woman came to Ibn Omar and said: “What do you say about silk? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is a mistake, and the one before it is more like the correct one. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9218","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ali bin Ghurab told us, he said: Behis bin Fahdan told us, he said: Abu Shaykh al-Hinai told us, he said: I heard Ibn Omar says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing silk.”"
"9219","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Shaykh, that he heard Muawiyah, and he had A group of the companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do you know that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade wearing silk?” They said: “Oh God, yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9220","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am An-Nadr bin Shumail, he said: Bayhas bin Fahdan told us, he said: Abu Shaykh al-Hinai told us, he said: I heard Muawiyah, and around him were people of the Muhajireen and Ansar, and he said to them: Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing Silk? They said: Oh God, yes"
"9221","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he is Ibn Kathir, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Sheikh Al-Hinai told me, on the authority of Abu Hamman, that Muawiyah, in the year of Hajj, gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in The Kaaba, and he said to them: “I adjure you by God, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid wearing silk? They said: Yes, he said: And I I bear witness (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9222","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abu Sheikh told me, On the authority of his brother Hamman, that Muawiyah, in the year of Hajj, gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the Kaaba, and he said to them: “ I adjure you by God, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid wearing silk? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness that he narrated it Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Shaykh Al-Hinai, on the authority of Jamaz, on the authority of Muawiyah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9223","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Saeed told us, he said: Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said : Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Abu Shaykh told me, he said: Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar in The Kaaba, and he said: “I adjure you by God, did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding silk clothes? They said: By God, yes. He said: I bear witness"
"9224","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Amara bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu told me Ishaq, he said: Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj and called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba, and said: “I adjure you by God, have you not heard the Messenger of Does God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbid silk? They said: Oh God, yes. He said: And I bear witness."
"9225","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid informed us, on the authority of Uqba bin Alqamah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, He said: Abu Ishaq told me, he said: Ibn Hamman told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of Ansar to the Kaaba, and he said: “I implore you By God, did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding silk clothes? They said: By God, yes. He said: And I bear witness?"
"9226","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, he said: he told me Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Humran told me, he said: Muawiyah performed Hajj, so he called a group of the Ansar to the Kaaba. He said: “I adjure you by God, did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbidding silk clothes?” They said: “By God, yes.” He said: And I bear witness.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Qatada has a better memory than Yahya bin Abi Kathir, and his hadith is more correct, and with God, success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9227","Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Safwan Al-Basri Al-Thaqafi informed us, saying: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa’id, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Dawud, such and such, Muhammad said: On the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever wears silk in this world, will not He will wear it in the Hereafter, and if he enters Paradise, the people of Paradise will wear it, and he will not wear it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is a mistake, but the correct thing is Daoud al-Sarraj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9228","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Dawud al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9229","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Shayban told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Daoud al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, He said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the hereafter.” Shu'bah said: Hisham said: Qatada reported this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sa`id ibn al-Faraj al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Daoud al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Saeed, his statement. Shu'bah said: Hisham told me, and he was more companionable to him than me, that he used to refer it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9230","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Daoud al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Saeed, The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and if he enters Paradise, the people of Paradise, and he did not wear it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9231","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd. Ibn Muqrin, on the authority of Al-Baraa, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do seven things, and forbade us to do seven things. He forbade us to do seven rings. “Gold, and silver vessels, and silk, and brocade, and brocade, and coir, and red, and copper.”"
"9232","Suleiman bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Single, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do seven things, and forbade us to do seven things: gold rings, silver vessels, and “Mathir, qisya, ivory, brocade, and silk.”"
"9233","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Salem bin Nuh told us, he said: Omar bin Amir told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that Ukaidir Duma was guided. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a robe of silk, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, put it on. The people were amazed at it, and he said: “Do you wonder? Who is this? By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Saad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than these. He gave them as a gift to Omar, and said: Oh. Messenger of God, you hate it and wear it!! He said: “O Umar, I have only sent it to you so that you may send it to a place where you may find it.” And that was before he forbade silk. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9234","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila . And Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila. And Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uqaym, said: Hudhayfah asked for water, and Dihqan brought him water in a silver vessel, so he drained it, then He apologized to them for what he had done to him, and said: I forbade it. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not drink from a vessel of gold. And silver, and do not wear brocade or silk, for it is for them in this world, and for us in the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9235","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Hafsa, That Atarid ibn Hajib brought a brocade garment that Khosrau had covered with it, and Umar said: Shall I not buy it for you, O Messenger of God? He said: “It is only worn by one who has no manners.”"
"9236","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, on the authority of Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Waqid bin Amr bin Saad. Bin Muadh, he said: I entered upon Anas bin Malik when he came to Medina, so I greeted him, and he said: Who are you from? I said: I am Waqid bin Amr bin Saad bin Muadh. He said: Saad was the greatest and tallest of people. Then he cried and cried more, so he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to Ukaidir, the owner of Douma in Quba, and he sent him a brocade robe woven with gold. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, put it on, then he got up on the pulpit and sat down. He did not speak and came down and made the people touch it with their hands. He said: “Are you amazed at this? The handkerchiefs of Saad bin Muadh in Paradise are better than what you see.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9237","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me that He heard Jabir say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wore a brocade cloak that had been given to him, then he was about to take it off, so he sent it to Omar. It was said to him: What you have almost removed, O Messenger of God. He said: “Gabriel, peace be upon him, forbade me from doing so.” Then Omar came crying, and said: O Messenger of By God, I hated something and you gave it to me. He said: “I did not give it to you to wear, but rather I gave it to you to sell.” So Omar sold it for two thousand dirhams. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9238","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya, who is the son of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Abdullah A servant of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, he said: “Asma’ brought out to me a garment made of woven brocade with a span of brocade made of serwan. And her private parts, meaning silk, were blind, so she said: This is the robe of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he died, it was with Aisha.”"
"9239","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Thana Surayj, he said: Thana Hushaym, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of my father, Asma’s freed slave, Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a robe made of yarn, made of brocade brocade.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is not preserved, and the one before it is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9240","Qutaibah told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, while he was on the pulpit giving a sermon, and he said: Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
